0.3.0 retargeted the plugin at the DeepSeek Harness 0.2.x plugin APIs:

  * the settings section is no longer registered by the plugin
    (`installSettingsSection` / `settingsNamespace` were removed from
    `@deepseek-ai/dsh-settings` in 0.1.7; forms are now derived from the
    profile entry and its exported `Config`);
  * session persistence is addressed through per-session handles
    (`sessionPersistence.open` / `create` + handle `read` / `append` / `flush`)
    instead of the retired service-level `load` / `append` pair.

0.4.0 reduced the package to a launcher: it opens the official
chat.deepseek.com web app in a window instead of driving the page and
re-rendering the conversation. The custom chat panel, the local transcript
store, the five `webchat_*` agent tools, the transfer/distillation code and
thirteen of the fifteen HTTP routes were removed, along with the
`playwright-core` runtime dependency and the React-based client build.

See MAINTAINING.md for the current structure and the constraints behind it.
